{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars","id":1049263,"title":"Thinking About 3e Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-15T06:16:40-08:00","id":1049263,"title":"Thinking About 3e Lunars","content":"So I guess a disclaimer that must be said is that I'm not necessarily looking for an argument about what Lunars should or should not be, but rather an examination of existing information and conversation to try to best understand what Lunars look like in 3rd Edition. The goal is that in assembling some baseline of ideas, it might help with homebrew that occurs on a minor level (QCs and other significant NPCs) as well as major ones, like people who might be interested in trying to write up the splat in 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of combing through the explanations offered by the Devs during the Q&amp;A sessions that happened early on (with an understanding that some of these things might be outdated or might have had their details changed), looking at the QCs that are currently in the corebook, and hopefully pondering or investigating other posts where the devs have shared some insight or thoughts on Lunars.<br /> <br /> I would appreciate it if we avoid getting really negative about the direction of the Lunars if it's something that anyone expresses apprehension over. I think the most valuable thing to do in this situation is to try to understand the consistent idea of Lunars being offered in 3rd Edition, as I certainly feel from my own exploration of these conversations that there <i>is </i>a consistent idea being expressed, even if some of its details have evolved over time. Try to keep it positive!<br /> <br /> To give an example of what I'm looking for, I'd love to engage in a conversation about the Lunar QCs in the 3rd Edition corebook. We can start with looking at the basics.<br /> <br /> <b>Lunar Excellencies</b><br /> The Lunar Excellency is pretty straightforward in how it can be powerful. Attribute is a solid pool that will usually be high for a Solar, nevermind a Lunar who might have slightly higher starting Attribute dots. That it doubles when stunted suggests two interesting things to me:<ul><li>Stunts are important here. In his excellent discussion of barbarism (thank you for writing that, Holden!) Holden mentioned that the aesthetic of barbarism and the like was a rich one that Lunars can draw upon to help differentiate themselves, and I find that to be really excellently rendered in an Excellency which engages with stunts. From a mechanical perspective, it also intrigues because it could be suggestive of how stunts like those described could also play a part in enhancing the mechanics of other Charms in the Lunar repertoire.</li> <li>A Lunar can take on a task where their Ability rating is very low, but possibly succeed at it through a canny stunt and raw dice power of their Excellency. This is cool, because if one doesn't fixate too much on the idea of Lunars being good generalists, the mechanics of the excellency are potentially suggestive of it. Similar to my mechanical note above, it also says, to me, that there's a great possibility of many Lunars being surprisingly capable of doing something which they might not have much natural training in.</li> <li>A small part of me is anxious about the idea of how to make Ability ratings into meaningful choices for the Lunar Exalted. Perhaps I've had too many critical discussions about charm sets for other types of Exalted which felt completely disconnected from what a person could actually do.</li> </ul>A sort of concluding thought is that, at its most basic, I know that Solars may reach for the greatest heights of power, but the Lunar Excellency lets them out on that playing field in a way that's really cool! I wonder how to describe their dice-caps though? As the Attribute in use x2? or would it simply be Attribute+Attribute used to stunt an action? A minor note that comes to mind is that it's probable that while they can throw around a lot of dice, they might hit the Solar dice-cap of 10 less often because of Attribute values being what they are and the degree to which it's feasible to always 'stack' your highest Attributes on an action.<br /> <br /> <b>Shapeshifting</b><br /> Oh man. One of my favorite superpowers in fiction, the shapeshifting of the Lunar Exalted pulls me to the splat in a lot of ways. Here are more opportunities for noticing some mechanical baselines.<br /> <br /> One thing that I feel should be said is that I don't get the impression that shapeshifting is actually the root expression of Lunar Charms. A very consistent impression I've gotten from the discussions I've seen from John lead me to believe this. It <i>does </i>seem however that it isn't absent from the charmset either. It strikes me that if we look at shapeshifting as a distinct <i>thing </i>associated with the Lunar Exalted, that we might look at it in the same way that some of the less skill-oriented Solar Exalted powers seem to be powers that we'd associate with the Unconquered Sun. That isn't to say that I expect all of the Lunar shapeshifting charms to be the apex of the charmset, but rather that these effects will be flavor or seasoning that accompanies themes primal power, raw cunning, that sort of thing. Ramble aside...<ul><li>Four motes to transform, just one short of what would lead to anima flare. A nice little detail. I wonder if Charms might potentially add to the cost of this while providing additional benefits? Could be good design space for Charms.</li> <li>The transformation lasts indefinitely. Cool! If you want to spend all your time as a raven, you totally can. I love that part of shapeshifters, where they can just chill out in an alternate shape.</li> <li>Transforming into your &quot;true human form&quot; is free and reflexive. That's an awesome touch. No mention of a spirit shape or anything here. A spirit shape is totally the kind of thing I would cut from a QC for the sake of word count, or because the team hasn't figured out how to tackle that issue again, but it will be interesting to see if that continues. I think it's a great way to give Lunars an additional shape at start and that the animal being connected to their personality is an awesome bit of aesthetic/informs a character in a really cool way, so it'll be very interesting to see how that's approached.</li> <li>Animal form grants access to all physical dicepools. This makes perfect sense when you're using QCs, and is a great way to simplify it for NPCs, but it does beg a small clarifying question: Do you choose to use their dice pools over yours in that form, or are you obligated to do so? I think from what I recall of reading <i>Manual of Exalted Power: Lunars </i>there were charms in 2e that you had to learn to 'choose' which stats to use when shapeshifted into that form. My gut is suggesting to me it's a choice, but I'm not 100% sure. If it is a choice it might be a nice way to remove what some might call exp tax or one of those mermaid problem charms.</li> <li>They get special attacks and merits of animals when using them. Awesome! Obviously these are the kinds of things which form the meat of having cool useful animal forms, but it's a great way for a Lunar to have some more diversity in his approach to his charms and abilities in combat. Plus, I don't recall that he <i>can't </i>use his Charms in conjunction with them.</li> <li>Latent or Magical abilities are not granted by shapeshifting, but can be unlocked via training and charms. Training them might work like spending EXP to grab them, possibly the amount you might spend training a pet or familiar to unlock them? That gives a cool experience way for someone to 'trick out' one of the animal forms they like to take. Using Charms to do it too is pretty cool, it reminds me of that Solar Occult Charm that let's Solars learn thaumaturgy rituals by committing motes. I could see a cool one like meditating with a bunch of birds to 'learn' and spend the motes to unlock it rather than Experience.</li> <li>Animals with Legendary Size are beyond the skill of most young Lunar Shapeshifters, but this limitation can be overcome. This brings us back to an age old conversation about the Tyrant Lizard Spirit Shape. Making it beyond the skill of most is intriguing, but it seems clear that if you really want to, you can overcome it. That does seem like a decent compromise. Sure, you might have the occasional Tyrant Lizard Lunar, but would it be good if they made it so that you couldn't have other big guys like the Mammoth or the Elephant? Or, god willing, the great and mighty <i>Yeddim Lunar? </i>I'm teasing around, but this seems fair enough.</li> <li>The Tell is such a cool ideas, and I'm glad to see it here. It doesn't really need to state here if it's like some kind of psychic effect or not, because word count and QC, but I wonder if they'll spend many words on it in the Lunars book. That somebody who is looking for it might spot it is pretty awesome, and a default difficulty of 7 is no joke. The Tell is another great way to give a character a certain visual flair.</li> </ul>One thing I note here is that you do <i>not </i>get the health levels of the animal you take the shape of. This makes good sense! Shifting HLs are already hard to deal with on their own. In addition to an Ox-Body, I can easily imagine a design space for gaining bonus temporary health levels when shapeshifted. It makes me wonder if broad criteria to activate powers like, &quot;shapeshifting into a large animal&quot; might be in there. It certainly feels appropriate with stunts being a big thing for their Excellency!<br /> <br /> It feels like a strong but basic set of guidelines for use. Great for the QCs, and leaving us with a number of intriguing questions.<br /> <br /> Going on from there, a look at a specific QC, one of the two we've got, the Barbarian Warlord!<br /> <br /> <b>Barbarian Warlord</b><br /> So this is the first QC. I will try to make specific observations about mechanics.<ul><li>Worshipped as a living god! So we see a Lunar among the barbarians in action. As Holden noted in his essay, it seems like even when he's fighting alongside a horde of barbarian people, he still exists as an other, a living god that they worship.</li> <li>He's Essence 2! For an Exalt, that's big news. Tough guy who has clearly been at it for awhile at least. That makes it slightly harder to tell if his Charms are all Essence 1 or 2, though! Oh no!</li> <li>The Shapeshifting section presents a Bear as his main animal form for combat. Could this then be a &quot;Spirit Shape&quot; or just the first one mentioned?</li> <li>He has a variety of forms, animal and human. No mention of other things, but that's cool.</li> <li><b>Deadly Beastman Transformation: </b>Holy <i>crap </i>that's scary! But wait, &quot;The Lunar may shapeshift into a ferocious battle form that is half-man, half-bear.&quot; That description of the Bear as his main form suddenly seems to lend credence to some kind of spirit or signature shape still existing... Which is cool. Clearly, it interacts with DBT, which I expect to be a Charm. Looking at the values, I'm intrigued... Glancing at his stats, I think that +4 to withering damage might be adding (Strength) to the withering attack damage. But maybe he has really high Dexterity? I dunno. The boost to Strength and qualifiers for Feats of Strength is definitely (Essence) which is really cool. Beware the Essence 5 Lunar! I suspect that, if DBT goes into the Charm tree, it might go into <b>Strength</b>. I considered Stamina, but suspect that is 3 rather than 4. I have a suspicion that this might be E2 DBT after getting a bunch of upgrades, namely halving Wound Penalties and healing damage conditionally. Maybe the (Essence) to Strength for feats of Strength could also be an upgrade charm, but because it's just for Feats of Strength, it might not be.</li> <li><b>Spine-Breaking Technique</b> this one is brutal. Really mess them up in a Grapple. I think this is an example of an effect that's a bit 'barbaric' or 'raw' but not necessarily rooted in the shapeshifting, and that Lunar Charms might look most often like this. I think this is a <b>Strength </b>Charm as well.</li> <li><b>Terrifying Bestial Visage </b>Charms which are conditionally activated on transformation! Awesome. He rolls 7 dice, which is likely a reference to his intimidation pool, and the successes are compared against Resolve <i>and </i>it acts as a command or rally action for the forces under the Lunar's control. So basically while shapeshifting they can get a social influence/command in at the same time. This is a neat charm, and a very powerful one! Since it has a specific condition for its activation, I think that might account for how this effect is used, because it's sort of limited by the amount of times you transform in a fight, and more notably, it's limited by <i>what you transform into</i>. This kind of conditional Charm usages seems like a great way to build a Lunar playstyle! I honestly have no idea what Attribute I'd peg this for. Charisma? Appearance? Intelligent? I suspect <b>Charisma </b>is the answer.</li> <li><b>Impenetrable Beast Armor </b>is this one literal or metaphorical? A straightforward and meaty defensive charm. Halving post-soak damage is a flat effect, but subtracting three dice from the raw damage? If we peek at his soak/hardness, I suspect the value here is (Stamina). I also would bet that this is a <b>Stamina </b>Charm. Whether one might call this a 'shapeshifting charm' is ambiguous to me, but I imagine it might be a bit metaphorical. It's very solid though! Lunar charms using Attribute values to boost things looks like it could be very scary, though.</li> </ul>That covers the Barbarian Warlord, and I might try to do a close look at the Trickster later. Overall, I actually do think these charms do a really decent job of conveying a distinct tone of Lunar power, and of showing interesting mechanical conditions that Lunar charms could be activated in. This is definitely speaking to the combat side of things.<br /> <br /> I remember reading one criticism that DBT felt like it was an obligatory pick up for Lunars in 2nd Edition, and I wonder how they'll do that here. It strikes me that at a glance, I feel like the bonus to withering damage and the bonus to Feats of Strength are probably the core of the charm, and that its other benefits might be upgrades, but that thinking might be wrong-headed. It's also worth noting that if some charms have conditional activations which require shapeshifting that it might be having the trade-off between using your DBT and losing out on those conditional charms, which could be one way to do it.<br /> <br /> For some reading outside of the corebook that might spark some conversation: <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">Holden on Barbarism</a><br /> <br /> That post by Holden is great not just for breaking down some complicated concepts that are gonna be engaged with by Lunars, but also gives a great little history of how they've been engaged with in previous editions. Knowing where they came from is definitely a part of trying to figure out how to not make the same mistakes, and it's generally a good read anyway.<br /> <br /> Eric Minton also did a great job collecting a number of bits from a conversation about Lunars on his blog. <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/09/27/lunar-exalted-what-are-they-to-you-thread-summary/\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Exalted: What Are They To You? Summary</a><br /> <br /> This has some old posts by a lot of members of the team talking about things. Some of it is a mite bit confusing, and perhaps talking through it might help all of us understand better?<br /> <br /> I completely understand that views on some of these things might've shifted in the intervening years, but I do still think there's value to be gleaned from these things, if you guys have any thoughts on any of this or things you want to add, please do! Lunars are very intriguing to me as someone who has <i>not </i>played a ton of Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:04:00-08:00","id":1049320,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on what Lunars will come to be in Third Edition align pretty strongly with these.<br /> <br /> I have a definite, strong image of them as dual-natured shapeshifting monstrous heroes based on how they've been portrayed in Ex3 so far and past discussions on their direction. And to me those elements suggest a very consistent picture of their charmset as being not predominantly about shapeshifting or animal power, but a conjunction of self-empowering shapeshifting and primal methodology and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-15-2017, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:46:22-08:00","id":1049435,"title":"","content":"Re: Excellencies 1) I think there might be more obvious syngeries between physical-physical attributes or mental-mental (&quot;I perform this action fast AND strong&quot;, &quot;I am charismatic AND beautiful&quot;) - would be interesting if I'm wrong, 2) I have a slight anxiety about the Excellency+Stunt =2x Attribute in that it seems like it puts a lot of potential dice weight on stunting, which could be less fun if it starts to cause obligate stunting / stunting fatigue (sorry, I know this is meant to be positive here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:09:37-08:00","id":1049471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1049435#post1049435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Excellencies 1) I think there might be more obvious syngeries between physical-physical attributes or mental-mental (&quot;I perform this action fast AND strong&quot;, &quot;I am charismatic AND beautiful&quot;) - would be interesting if I'm wrong, 2) I have a slight anxiety about the Excellency+Stunt =2x Attribute in that it seems like it puts a lot of potential dice weight on stunting, which could be less fun if it starts to cause obligate stunting / stunting fatigue (sorry, I know this is meant to be positive here).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the threshold for needing the second Attribute is similar to the threshold for Anima Flare and the round/hourly mote regen. So if you're trying to be subtle or stealthy in any way, or trying to conserve motes, you're not going to be reaching for it anyway. But it's there for when you need to go all in, and I'd expect an extravagant stunt then anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T12:51:02-08:00","id":1181472,"title":"","content":"First and foremost, is there any hopethey won't suck in 3rd ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T19:40:10-08:00","id":1181553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1049435#post1049435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Excellencies 1) I think there might be more obvious syngeries between physical-physical attributes or mental-mental (&quot;I perform this action fast AND strong&quot;, &quot;I am charismatic AND beautiful&quot;) - would be interesting if I'm wrong, 2) I have a slight anxiety about the Excellency+Stunt =2x Attribute in that it seems like it puts a lot of potential dice weight on stunting, which could be less fun if it starts to cause obligate stunting / stunting fatigue (sorry, I know this is meant to be positive here).</div> </div> </div> </div>First don't think these stunts need to be terribly complex as adding perception or dexterity to a roll you just needs you to say 'with precision ____ does _____'<br /> <br /> That said I think that the stunt requirement is important so that the stats added make sense, and if people are taking more than 30 seconds stunting you've got a differnt problem. 'I swing my axe into his gut' is a perfectly servicable stunt after all. Rank 1 sure, but that's all a lunar needs anyway for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16904-cold-burn","name":"Cold Burn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16904_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T04:56:44-08:00","id":1181619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1181472#post1181472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost, is there any hopethey won't suck in 3rd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always hope. From the sounds of it, the current devs at least have a strong thematic and aesthetic image of the Lunar Exalted. Of course, since everyone has their own idea of what the Lunars should be, it remains to be seen if that image falls out well with the community. I think there's a better chance of them coming out decent if there's a unified image behind them, though. Can't please everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T05:36:45-08:00","id":1181628,"title":"","content":"Lunars at my table will <b>not</b> suck. Rawr, baby.<br /> <br /> I'm working up, at a very beginning stage yet, an interlocking set of Shapeshifting, Anima/Caste, and Lair Knacks. And cogitating on how the tattoo Evocations will work with them. And how the Solar relationship works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T05:59:45-08:00","id":1181632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1181628#post1181628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars at my table will <b>not</b> suck. Rawr, baby.<br /> Shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually got criticized. Like, it's broken and barely useful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&gt;And how the Solar relationship works.<br /> Also afraid of this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Other things (experience and skills focus) being equal, can Lunars fight on equals with Solars at 2(L)-to-1(S)? And with Abyssals at 3-to-1?<br /> <br /> P.S. How can you work with this, since the book isn't there yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:03:21-08:00","id":1181639,"title":"","content":"Dude, shapeshifting is incredibly useful. I'm currently playing an essence 4 Solar after playing a Lunar for years, and I keep thinking &quot;man, I wish I could turn into a bird/spider/fly/tyrant lizard right now&quot;. <br /> But I can't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And it'll be even better this edition (except for people with tyrant lizard or elephant totems, but I think we can all agree that's a good thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:05:02-08:00","id":1181640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cold Burn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1181553#post1181553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First don't think these stunts need to be terribly complex as adding perception or dexterity to a roll you just needs you to say 'with precision ____ does _____'<br /> <br /> That said I think that the stunt requirement is important so that the stats added make sense, and if people are taking more than 30 seconds stunting you've got a differnt problem. 'I swing my axe into his gut' is a perfectly servicable stunt after all. Rank 1 sure, but that's all a lunar needs anyway for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reflecting back on this, I think you and Handigar are both correct - players probably won't be drawing for the big Attribute+Attribute limits that frequently and it won't be so required to be viable to achieve that it becomes a burden, and the stunt requirement should be simple enough (&quot;I swing my axe powerfully!&quot;) that it doesn't create huge disparities between players with a great visual imagination and those with less of one.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of &quot;at your table thing&quot; though, so perhaps they'll give more guidance in the book as it could be important for balance (if I think of the Excellency type Charms as pretty important as the broad &quot;engine room&quot; baseline for the splats that greatly influence the efficacy of what the downstream Charms can achieve).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:09:19-08:00","id":1181644,"title":"","content":"I'd be tempted to just let players always add strength on their attacks, so as not to hear them desperately trying to find the 11th synonym for &quot;I swing my axe powerfully&quot;.<br /> <br /> We've been playing with Lunars based off the antagonist rules for a while, and honestly, I find it a bit irritating. It does slow things down to say a stunt and then keep asking &quot;can I add my X to the cap?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:41:33-08:00","id":1181656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1181472#post1181472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost, is there any hopethey won't suck in 3rd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very loaded question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:13:28-08:00","id":1181663,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> thanks for the actual play perspective on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T09:07:24-08:00","id":1181677,"title":"","content":"After posting it, I realised that it may not apply to everyone.<br /> When I first started playing Exalted, I thought stunting was really cool. And we used to stunt basically everything.<br /> <br /> But having played tons and tons of Exalted, when in combat, we really just want it to go along at a quick pace, and not get slowed down by going back and forth by asking about stunt bonuses (2nd ed required constant 2-dice stunts, which got rather annoying).<br /> <br /> And I myself basically don't give out stunt bonuses for flips, because... so... many... ****ing flips... it's just not exciting any more.<br /> <br /> There's one guy who thinks of really cool stunts in combat, but everyone else doesn't care. It's something to do when you want to eke out another few dice on occasion, not something to do on every combat action.<br /> <br /> In fact, the guy playing the Changing Moon essentially never, ever stunts (except when it's a social action, because saying &quot;I use social stuff on them&quot; rather than actually saying what you're saying, is pretty lame). He certainly never asks for stunt bonuses.<br /> <br /> So that's the environment that we're using this rule.<br /> <br /> If you have a group who are really keen on stunts and still love them, as we did once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also say, don't take this as me saying new Lunars are terrible. Other than that, I'm happy with pretty much everything we've seen so far, both mechanically and fluff-wise. The only other mechanical issues we've had is the general issues of using QC stats (ie there's some rolls there's no dice for, we weren't sure about how they interact with dice caps, etc), but that's likely to get cleared up in the book (Vance has already commented on the dice caps).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T10:09:49-08:00","id":1181697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1181632#post1181632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually got criticized. Like, it's broken and barely useful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&gt;And how the Solar relationship works.<br /> Also afraid of this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Other things (experience and skills focus) being equal, can Lunars fight on equals with Solars at 2(L)-to-1(S)? And with Abyssals at 3-to-1?<br /> <br /> P.S. How can you work with this, since the book isn't there yet</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An excellent question! I'm working with it <i>because </i>the book isn't there yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's a set of homebrew charms, which I've browsed a bit. And I have the 1st and 2nd Ed books for ideas. My main line of scribble-scrabble right now is in a non-Attribute-based on how I'd like things to work, plus the (very interesting and open-ended) idea of Evocations, as deeper magics that build upon basic ones. Basically, breaking out as much as I can from the existing ideas of the Charm trees.<br /> <br /> In the past, we had a 2nd Ed game where the Lunars kept up with the Solaroids very well. (Disclosure: I portray Solaroids, Lunars, Sidereals all as co-equal, co-awesome, but different-niche Celestials.) Some Charms in Ink Monkeys had to be excluded (I punch you 50 miles away!) but not too many.<br /> <br /> Lunars did need some careful Charm-choosing thought, while the Solar players could be pretty carefree in picking them.<br /> <br /> The worst issues we had in that game were our Infernal character running away with the show, and our Sidereal character who was completely buried in broken speedbumpy Charms he had to buy. The latter became an NPC.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, keeping in mind that this is coming from my own scribbles that I've barely gotten out of my head and into OneNote...<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting is the intended default mode for Lunars to Get Things Done. A basic Shapeshift costs 1 mote - this puts it in line with Excellent Strike. I'm picking on Excellent Strike because it's a presumably automatic effect that Solars do - better economics than Excellency, and priced to encourage you to do so often. I anticipate that a proper Shapeshift should add dice for the duration of the Scene or the Shapeshift, as a persistent effect. It would be really nice if I had a guideline ready, but I don't.<br /> <br /> Buying into more Shapeshifting Knacks gives you more access to different things, which can also drive the cost up.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting comes with free Elsewhere storage for your Stuff. There ought to be a Knack for Big Stuff.<br /> <br /> DBT will (I'm hoping) be an optional combat style for Lunars who prefer to build a <i>damn awesome</i> combat mode and stick with it, instead of constantly shifting around.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting in general is harmonious with Changing Moon Caste. DBT and its Gifts are harmonious with Full Moon Caste as well. Ghosts, demons, Raksha, gods, and the aspects thereof are also harmonious with No Moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All of the Territory stuff goes into Lair. I'm totally copying my homework from Beast, here. If you have a Lair, you have a Heart. Unless you expand on it, it's the Elsewhere zone where all of your shapes and Stuff are present. You can go and visit them if you have the proper Charms. Sometimes they'll talk to you and it will be really creepy.<br /> <br /> If you do expand on it, each expansion lets you take over a Lair in a territory somewhere. To do so, you become the apex predator/monster/master in the area. This may be social or craft or occult. Or it may be a Proper Lunar Beatdown.<br /> <br /> When you're the apex, the territory is yours. You can appear and vanish from the Lair entrance there, and use your burrows to quickly travel around. You can gain Intimacies, empower Charms, and fast-travel this way. This is the Lunarity equivalent of high-speed Solar travel and political dominance.<br /> <br /> Also note that there's a hint of the Solar-Lunar dynamic here. The Solar would be the natural king or queen of a territory, while the Lunar could be the legendary monster nearby. This could be a spousal relationship like was expected in 1st and 2nd Ed. It could be hostile, or mentoring, or protective. Or it could be entirely out of whack and Limit-whammied. To the mortals nearby, the Solar &amp; Lunar could be the hero-monster pair of myth, just as easily as they could be partners.<br /> <br /> You can link up your Lair Chambers to other Lunars' (or other gods, etc, if they agree), and the Lunars themselves have a project to build Moon Paths all around Creation and beyond. The project is going poorly, but it gets them around the worst of the Wyld Hunt and the Loom of Fate's predictions.<br /> <br /> Territory in general is harmonious with Full Moon Caste. Territory in a civilized area is also harmonious with Changing Moon Caste. Territory Way Out There is also harmonious with No Moon Caste.<br /> <br /> (Rumors that an ancient and cruel Solar forged the first Anathema Dagger to use against his Lunar mate in her Heart chamber, for fear that she could retreat there out of his grasp, are certainly no more than cautionary tales told to young Lunars. Yep. Definitely.)<br /> <br /> (There's more hiding in here too. A Lunar Lair can easily be a &quot;magical world&quot; in a Campbell-style hero's journey. Also, I'm pondering a sort of Hurry Home as an emergency escape, in the style of the Sidereal ceasing to exist Charm.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lunar understanding and manipulation of mysteries, lore, occult, crafting, and so on, I'm putting in a tree for Lunar Circle Sorcery. Though that name is grossly inaccurate and just a placeholder. I pretty much picked that name with the intent that it will lead to a capstone power of sorts.<br /> <br /> This will include all of the related Charms that don't really map to a particular Attribute. Plus it will have all of the ways to travel to faraway places and survive there.<br /> <br /> I'm anticipating a high-level type of working, which is what inspired the temporary name. This will cover all of the great Lunar miracles, such as saving the Castes from further dissolving, creating the tattoos, creating the Charms and Knacks other Lunars use for Territory and Lair, and so on. The main difference is that the Lunar, themselves, becomes what they are creating - temporarily or permanently; or they otherwise breed it or inspire it as a legend until it takes root and becomes true.<br /> <br /> A Lunar who wants to create a Daiklaive, for instance, might start by talking up the legend of the terrible monster wielding it. It might draw some interest as mortals and Exalted go to find it, only to go missing. As the legend starts to take shape, the intended weapon might appear in his hand, long enough for the Lunar himself to appear (as that terrible monster) and defeat a Circle come to claim it. Finally, it takes shape permanently, when the working is complete.<br /> <br /> Creating a Manse might involve becoming the various gods of the area, enough to adjust some dragon lines. Then taking on the shapes of the land, buildings, and other features, a bit at a time, until the Essence of the area starts to hold the shape on its own.<br /> <br /> The greatest miracles would be the final workings of Lunars who devote themselves entirely into their completion. The mystery of tattoo creation, repairing the Castes, and so on, each has the soul and Heart of a Lunar hidden inside them.<br /> <br /> This is by far the least-drafted bit of what I have in mind. I just started this week. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This Sorcery in general is harmonious with No Moon Caste. Something in here would be harmonious with each of Full Moon and Changing Moon Castes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Caste will absorb all the ideas of renown, as well as Anima and other non-Charm benefits.<br /> <br /> As a Lunar grows and excels in each of the three areas above (Sorcery, Lair, Shapeshifting) they gain benefits relating to that Caste.<br /> <br /> [Edit to add: The intent is that a Full Moon warrior will be your straightforward Werewolf or Were-X , with emphasis on shifting into a defined and ever-growing War Form to Get Stuff Done - the War Form would be something greater than its parts, unique, powerful and terrifying. A Changing Moon trickster will be the face-borrowing, skinchanging, Beast Boy, Zan and Zane type master shapeshifter - they wouldn't be able to impersonate a Destiny (that's for Sids) but they could build fake lives and steal faces and bodies. A No Moon witch will be the monster under your bed, ethereal, shadowed, and knowing of all things hidden - and who create magic of and through themselves. This post is a horrendous scrambled mess of the ideas I'm going for!]<br /> <br /> Un-tattooed Lunars would have the full benefits of the Caste matching the phase of the moon, and including all of the rewnown-like progress within that Caste. They wouldn't get much else that tattooed Lunars get (as below) but also wouldn't have to sink XP into it either. Each time they see the moon for the first time in a night, they may choose three of the (about five) perks in that phase's Caste.<br /> <br /> Tattoed Lunars gain three perks (out of maybe five to choose from) in their fixed Caste. Those are also fixed.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Tattoos however, can gain Evocations of their own, which interact with Caste, Anima, and other things.<br /> <br /> Tattoed Artifacts (armor, for instance) may be Evoked as needed, which is rather expensive. They may be evoked permanently, which is less expensive but committed forever. Or they may be evoked as part of DBT Gifts, which is relatively cheap and obvious and becomes a built-in part of their DBT. Each one will be only Evoked one way, unless maybe you alter that later by buying in to further Evocations of that Artifact.<br /> <br /> At about Essence 2, you can start gaining the other perks of your assigned Caste. Only three can be active at a time, but you can choose them each time you see the moon (in any phase) for the first time in a night. Each additional one you gain is an Evocation of the tattoos.<br /> <br /> At about Essence 3, you can start gaining perks from other Castes. They are also Evocations. You can only have one Caste's perks at a time, even if you only have the one.<br /> <br /> At about Essence 5, the Lunar begins to realize the totality of the Changing Gift, and may start to mix-n-match perks that they know.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 02-02-2018, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T19:31:16-08:00","id":1182476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1181628#post1181628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how the Solar relationship works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of having it be a Flaw, <a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/12548572/chapters/29647464\" target=\"_blank\">as I've written out here.</a><br /> <br /> What mechanic are you looking at?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:04:14-08:00","id":1182480,"title":"","content":"Put me in the camp of people who is kind of annoyed with how the excellency seems to work, for two main reasons.<br /> <br /> The first has already been mentioned which is when you do want to go all out you have to be constantly coming up with new reasons why your lunar can use their 5 stamina to attack or 5 manipulation to solve a intelligence check. As the DM I have found this to really slow down game play when I am trying to use a lunar npc.<br /> <br /> The second is (assuming lunars get they same number of attribute dots as solars) your attribute pools are going to be way lower than your ability pools. So a lunar trying to use their secondary/tertiary attributes is either going to be adding between 2-3 dice to it or bump into problem one of constantly trying to shove their highest attribute into every single test.<br /> <br /> My other issue with the NPC in the corebook and one in which I disagree with the OP about is that their charms as presented feel rather bland.<br /> <br /> They are not weak but I found they do not convey they same distinct flavor of the exalt in the same way the DB's sidereal and liminals ones do. This will likely be fixed with the final charm set but it did kind of leave my players with a poor first impression of the splat.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T02:43:10-08:00","id":1182525,"title":"","content":"I very much agree with you about the first point, but not the second point.<br /> <br /> I find Lunars tend to have very high attributes: unlike Solars, they put a fair amount of XP into them, but also because of freebies.<br /> <br /> Without much need to boost abilities, favoured attributes traditionally at 3 points a dot, and now tertiary attributes also at 3pts a dot, it's very easy to go &quot;hmmm... what to do with my 15 freebie points. I guess I'll buy 5 extra dots of attributes.&quot;<br /> Or at least 4 and a few dots of backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Also, Lunars have always started with slightly more attribute dots and slightly less ability dots than Solars, which I imagine will continue.<br /> <br /> My Essence 4 No Moon had 7 attributes at 5 (and one at 4, and one at 3).<br /> Obviously that's at essence 4, not essence 1, but I think starting Lunars tend to have quite a lot of dots too.<br /> <br /> Certainly, &quot;Attribute+Attribute&quot; for an Attribute-based Exalt seems more advantageous to me than &quot;Attribute+Ability&quot; for an ability-based Exalt. <br /> <br /> <br /> As to the charms... I thought they were okay. Not amazing, but decent. Though the 2nd ed Lunar charmset isn't hard to beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T04:13:02-08:00","id":1182538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182476#post1182476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of having it be a Flaw, <a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/12548572/chapters/29647464\" target=\"_blank\">as I've written out here.</a><br /> <br /> What mechanic are you looking at?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of giving it some Merit points or even a Charm-like tree of suggested benefits. Know how to find each other, instant communication, perfect combat coordination if you really go all-in on it. That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Each partner would have to buy in the same amount and in the same benefits, or it simply doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse lurks in this relationship though. At some point in the story (If and only if the players are into the idea), one or the other of them would discover ways to unbalance the relationship. Perhaps taking extra dots or Charm-likes, when the other hasn't taken ones to match. The more unbalanced it goes, the more troubled the relationship becomes. Maybe that should be Limit, or maybe Curse-twisted Intimacies if we need mechanics for it. Maybe it only manifests if one partner reincarnates, and re-Exalts without enough Relationship Stuff to balance it.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of stories that can come out of this, so I like having ideas and options. But, it flirts with the Red Rule so I hesitate to make it mandatory.<br /> <br /> Just thinking it through with my own group...<br /> ... I have a married couple who play, who would very likely jump on an in-game partnership. They always make up partnered characters anyway.<br /> ... I have a player who likes stories with relationship or familial status. Things like being a noble and dealing with noble courtship and politics.<br /> ... I have a player who enjoys challenging and difficult situations, and would probably like finding out that a reincarnated mate has gone evil this time.<br /> ... and I have a player who enjoys playing sarcastic troublemakers (in character) just outside the idea-space of the rest of the group, who would probably be disinterested in doing the mate thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit to add] I really like how you lay it out as None/Minor/Major/Defining and use the Flaw mechanic to provide XP. I might build up on my idea based on following the Intimacy levels like you did, with a Flaw coming out of it for going off-balance. Awesome food for thought, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 02-05-2018, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T04:45:09-08:00","id":1182542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182480#post1182480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put me in the camp of people who is kind of annoyed with how the excellency seems to work, for two main reasons.<br /> <br /> The first has already been mentioned which is when you do want to go all out you have to be constantly coming up with new reasons why your lunar can use their 5 stamina to attack or 5 manipulation to solve a intelligence check. As the DM I have found this to really slow down game play when I am trying to use a lunar npc.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I hope I got the quote cut correctly, let's find out!)<br /> <br /> Thinking on this one, I believe I'd let my Lunars invoke their second-Attribute might once per Scene or Shapeshift to establish it, and then generally let it ride. <br /> <br /> The goal of the Stunting mechanic is to encourage players to help build up the Scene. When it becomes neutral or detrimental to that goal, it's time to rethink!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182480#post1182480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second is (assuming lunars get they same number of attribute dots as solars) your attribute pools are going to be way lower than your ability pools. So a lunar trying to use their secondary/tertiary attributes is either going to be adding between 2-3 dice to it or bump into problem one of constantly trying to shove their highest attribute into every single test.<br /> <br /> My other issue with the NPC in the corebook and one in which I disagree with the OP about is that their charms as presented feel rather bland.<br /> <br /> They are not weak but I found they do not convey they same distinct flavor of the exalt in the same way the DB's sidereal and liminals ones do. This will likely be fixed with the final charm set but it did kind of leave my players with a poor first impression of the splat.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The other side of that is that there are only 9 Attributes to cover all situations, vs. 28 Abilities. Solars and especially DB's benefit from specializing into Abilities (and the specialties of Abilities), while Lunars can be rather more broad-based. (Sids used a different Excellency mechanic entirely and I'd really have to reread what we know on Liminals to comment)<br /> <br /> Lunar combat Charms, also, work (*) on any combat Ability. The same Charm can enhance shooting a bow, throwing a boulder, punching somebody, or axing him to stop bothering you. A Melee Solar will want to get you into Melee, and if he does, he will probably win. But a Lunar could fight him by making sure it's either a long-range fight or a grapple.<br /> <br /> Lunars also get (*) Attribute bonuses based on their current Shapeshift. It's been a while since I reviewed this part, but I seem to recall they counted as Charm dice but you didn't have to pay for them after the initial Shapeshifting. So if you gain 3 Strength from being a gorilla, that's the same as 3 free Strength Excellency every action until you're tired of it.<br /> <br /> DBT and Spirit Shape also count (*) as a True Shape, so excellency limits track to follow them. Been workin' out, bruh?<br /> <br /> (*) or worked/got/counted, as of 2nd Edition<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T06:59:09-08:00","id":1182583,"title":"","content":"So, question for fellow Lunars fans...<br /> <br /> What are some Lunar story ideas or themes you particularly like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T05:58:16-08:00","id":1184350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182583#post1182583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question for fellow Lunars fans...<br /> <br /> What are some Lunar story ideas or themes you particularly like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Monster Hunter that seeks out ever-bigger and meaner beasts to kill, consuming them to absorb their power.<br /> <br /> <br /> The dragon who regards his loved ones as his treasures. Fiercely territorial for and protective of his chosen home, his chosen people, his chosen mate.<br /> <br /> <br /> The demigod whose athlete-slow heartbeats are loud and clear as thunderclaps when he begins to awaken the totality of his power for the fight ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /> The hero who becomes a kaiju.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T20:14:20-08:00","id":1185001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182583#post1182583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question for fellow Lunars fans...<br /> <br /> What are some Lunar story ideas or themes you particularly like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Eternal Enemy. <br /> <br /> A mysterious teacher that always seems to escape Realm\u2019s grasp at the last instant, he makes statements by becoming the legendary and feared monster they make him out to be. <br /> <br /> In his eyes, he\u2019s doing them a favour. He sees his eternal campaign against the empire as a school of Martial Arts of sorts. Every once in a generation the Enemy comes out of his hiding place and bites at the heels of the Realm hard enough so that they can\u2019t ignore the threat and mobilize. When he finally gets the battle he\u2019s craving for, his campaign turns into a long protracted guerilla warfare, a contorted lesson plan. Ultimately, his *pupils* have to make a sacrifice to win the day. He teaches lessons by training his enemies in the arts of what it means to survive him.<br /> <br /> The trainees survive to hear others sing of their heroism, all the while being haunted by the tough choices they had to make on the battlefield. It is only then that they understand their sifu. This is how the Eternal Enemy makes friends.<br /> <br /> In a sense, his true form is that of the curse of the war.<br /> <br /> <br /> He also happens to be an antagonist in the current game I\u2019m running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","name":"VX3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar81_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T12:02:20-08:00","id":1185683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182583#post1182583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question for fellow Lunars fans...<br /> <br /> What are some Lunar story ideas or themes you particularly like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite fond of the asymmetrical Cold War between the various Lunar factions and the Realm/Bronze Faction that the Devs bring up every so often. A proxy war between primal masters who can bring the fury of Nature itself to bear, versus those who command the most civilized portions of Creation not only brings to bear their barbarism, but also that perhaps neither side is truly right, something which I thought was absent in 2e's lore on Lunars. Now, I know that the Thousand Streams River is not remembered fondly here, but I also find this aspect of 3e Lunars appealing because it lets me play a bit with those ideas once again, except with a bit more focus. Rather than just &quot;Make the BEST society I can,&quot; it becomes, &quot;Make a warrior culture to use as a hammer to smash the Realm!&quot;<br /> <br /> Eh, I know that's probably not the most popular opinion, but I'm excited, hopefully naively for 3e Lunars because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T14:04:58-08:00","id":1185721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182583#post1182583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are some Lunar story ideas or themes you particularly like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Change on a deeply personal and arguably petty level. Lunars make the best dramatic heroes, because change is fundamentally tied to their core identity. Lunars who have to change something about themselves <i>as people</i>, completely independently of their shining silver demigod status, I think, should be a driving force of Lunar narratives.<br /> <br /> Lunars as paranoia fuel. Demigods with strange and monstrous powers who can be anyone, at any time. They know your deepest, darkest secrets. They can kill your loved ones and take their shape. The Lunar who is a ten foot tall kaiju monster is the safest Lunar, because you know where they are and what to expect from them.<br /> <br /> Lunars as witches for whom otherworldly insights and understanding is as natural as breathing. A Solar sorcerer comprehends the magics that flow through the world; a Lunar <i>feels</i> them. Also, the intersection of sorcery and the Lunar aesthetics of primal physicality: haruspicy, bloody rituals, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T00:00:14-08:00","id":1186199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1182480#post1182480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put me in the camp of people who is kind of annoyed with how the excellency seems to work, for two main reasons.<br /> The first has already been mentioned which is when you do want to go all out you have to be constantly coming up with new reasons why your lunar can use their 5 stamina to attack or 5 manipulation to solve a intelligence check. As the DM I have found this to really slow down game play when I am trying to use a lunar npc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it originally because involving different attributes more seemed like a great way to distinguish Lunar excellence from Solar excellence.<br /> I've gained some reservations about it after seeing people say things like how they intend to try and use one particular attribute to boost every roll of consequence which reminds me of the keywords of the Infernal Excellencies in a bad way where the memorable/exploitable keywords got overused and turned the Yozis into dumb memes of themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T02:50:27-08:00","id":1186220,"title":"","content":"I guess my point on that is that if the mechanics are set up such that Lunar player feel that they have to have these Solar sized dicepools to survive and stay secure in combat and other venues of action, then I wouldn't really blame players for cheap, continuous and unfun stunting to exploit an attribute. <br /> <br /> While if the mechanics are set up so they don't really need those dicepools, then they won't do it, generally.<br /> <br /> So either way it's first and foremost a mechanics thing and not a &quot;Bad audience is why we can't have nice things&quot; thing. (A mechanics thing I pretty much would trust the current designers to playtest and consider and to have the ability to be objective about and make a decision on, just to be clear, in case for some reason in someone's mind that was actually necessary for me to clarify.)<br /> <br /> This thread kind of has some suggestions it could go either way - only play evidence so far is Wizard sounds like he has had this kind of issue in his game, but then he's working with incomplete mechanics and he's admitted his group has stunting fatigue.<br /> <br /> (I mean, we're not talking some corner-case, obscure, Jon Chung exploit that the designers couldn't possibly be expected to predict during their quest to innocently give fun mechanics. This is like the most basic consequences of the mechanic.)<br /> <br /> (Same way if the Infernal Excellencies had problems in terms of depicting the Yozis which emerged through use in play, those problems are really the fault of the design, and how those excellencies were inevitably going to be used in play, rather than how players chose to use them. Though I'd suspect much of those arguable problems were really from people, including Michael Goodwin and Holden as the designers and with their enthusiasm, theorycrafting on the Excellencies and not how they were actually used in play. So it's a slightly distinct issue.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:33:09-08:00","id":1186652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1186199#post1186199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked it originally because involving different attributes more seemed like a great way to distinguish Lunar excellence from Solar excellence.<br /> I've gained some reservations about it after seeing people say things like how they intend to try and use one particular attribute to boost every roll of consequence which reminds me of the keywords of the Infernal Excellencies in a bad way where the memorable/exploitable keywords got overused and turned the Yozis into dumb memes of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does tend to inherit those issues from the stunting rules themselves. IME I've found that you can limit that just by asking players not to overdo it, and reminding them that not even Solars make <i>every </i>roll at base 10+10 dice. Also the groups I play in generally let you assume a 1-point stunt if you put any amount of description into the action at all instead of just saying &quot;I attack&quot; or &quot;I dodge&quot;. On the STing side of things, it helps to not give every single opponent maxed-out stats such that characters <i>need </i>to throw 20 dice as a baseline to have any chance of success.<br /> <br /> Generally, I've found that Exalted, more than other games, relies on good-faith agreements between the ST and the players to throttle the action and allow for pacing and tension, especially since it's very possible to max out the stats you care about at chargen, such that the only form of advancement left is charm buys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T09:18:28-08:00","id":1186691,"title":"","content":"I wholeheartedly agree about the good-faith implicit in a game like Exalted. <br /> <br /> For stunting, that means a fair assessment by the ST of a stunt's value. For a player, that means keeping basically in line with what Charms and abilities you can actually have. For both, it means using the stunting mechanics as a game reward for improving the narrative, and stepping back when they become tedious. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T16:16:24-08:00","id":1186861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1186199#post1186199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked it originally because involving different attributes more seemed like a great way to distinguish Lunar excellence from Solar excellence.<br /> I've gained some reservations about it after seeing people say things like how they intend to try and use one particular attribute to boost every roll of consequence which reminds me of the keywords of the Infernal Excellencies in a bad way where the memorable/exploitable keywords got overused and turned the Yozis into dumb memes of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be a bit more bookkeeping than some people like, but an idea I had for this is to just remove the need for a stunt and let people add a second attribute to the roll, but they have to cycle through which category the attribute comes from (IE: Rolling attack three turns in a row. Turn one, add strength. Turn two, add intelligence. Turn Three, add charisma.) The idea being, if you want 10 extra dice on every roll, you will need to invest heavily on attributes across multiple types of attributes. The other thing I speculate this might do is make for a fighting style that is evocative of the changing face of Luna. One which cycles and calls upon elements of physical prowess, mysticism, and trickery regardless of the situation at hand.<br /> <br /> The other idea I have, and I just have to wait to see if the devs have the same one, is to make it so that certain charms are tied to whether you are stunting a specific attribute in or not. Making it so you get different, valuable benefits from charms tied to a range of attributes could discourage a player from sitting on a single 5 + 5 combo and actually branch out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T16:49:04-08:00","id":1186868,"title":"","content":"Just gonna double post because this touches on a different topic. I think it would be interesting if the Solar Bond, the Lunar Tattoos are different means to the same end: Caste Fixing. The way I would explain it would be something like this. Lunars used their oaths to a Solar and the deliberative to affirm what they were in the face of their mutable nature, they tied their mercurial existence to an immovable golden pillar. When that pillar was torn down, for the first time in history, they were faced with the conundrum of being unable to fix their Castes and were faced with the nightmarish possibility of Chimerism. The Lunars created moonsilver tattoos as an alternative to the Solar Bond, but they were never intended to be given out to anybody. Instead, they were an offer you cannot refuse to get people to sign on to the Silver Pact. So, for a thousand years new Lunars received the not really a choice of &quot;sign up with Furry Isis and their war against China-Rome and the Astrology Jedis&quot; or &quot;succumb to Chimerism.&quot; Now, with the return of the Solars, they have a third option. They can renew their bond with the Solars and fix their Castes as they were meant to once more. Of course, now, it really is a choice. Those who wish to ignore the draw of their bond can do so easily. When they feel the call, they can ignore it and continue living their lives as if they never had a Solar Bond in the first place. But still, this would work to provide a serious reason for Lunars to want to be with their Solar mates beyond creepy mind control. Lunars get the choice between being at the beck and call of their Elders or their Partner - and there isn't really a right choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T19:31:50-08:00","id":1186907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1186868#post1186868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just gonna double post because this touches on a different topic. I think it would be interesting if the Solar Bond, the Lunar Tattoos are different means to the same end: Caste Fixing. The way I would explain it would be something like this. Lunars used their oaths to a Solar and the deliberative to affirm what they were in the face of their mutable nature, they tied their mercurial existence to an immovable golden pillar. When that pillar was torn down, for the first time in history, they were faced with the conundrum of being unable to fix their Castes and were faced with the nightmarish possibility of Chimerism. The Lunars created moonsilver tattoos as an alternative to the Solar Bond, but they were never intended to be given out to anybody. Instead, they were an offer you cannot refuse to get people to sign on to the Silver Pact. So, for a thousand years new Lunars received the not really a choice of &quot;sign up with Furry Isis and their war against China-Rome and the Astrology Jedis&quot; or &quot;succumb to Chimerism.&quot; Now, with the return of the Solars, they have a third option. They can renew their bond with the Solars and fix their Castes as they were meant to once more. Of course, now, it really is a choice. Those who wish to ignore the draw of their bond can do so easily. When they feel the call, they can ignore it and continue living their lives as if they never had a Solar Bond in the first place. But still, this would work to provide a serious reason for Lunars to want to be with their Solar mates beyond creepy mind control. Lunars get the choice between being at the beck and call of their Elders or their Partner - and there isn't really a right choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it wouldn't be the same end, according to the tone used in the book. The Lunars changed. They aren't the Lunars of the First Age or the wars that came before it, because the loss of the Solars tore away something that could never be replaced.<br /> <br /> Edit: And chimerism doesn't seem to enter into the equation, because it's just mixing features on your totem animal. It's totally cool with just about every Lunar, and not a gateway to madness in this edition.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the developers have expressed dissatisfaction with framing the Silver Pact as something similar to Daesh. The parallels aren't really there; they grind up Artifacts that they can't use because otherwise they would die in droves. They're more a parallel of some theoretical faction in Mad Max that blows up old tanks and warheads and destroys fuel because they're really good at fighting without them, so they take advantage of this. Those Lunars of a more preservative bent, meanwhile, strike me as being kind of like ComStar from BattleTech, which hoarded technological secrets to try and keep together some semblance of interstellar relations going but would also covertly sabotage and/or co-opt the efforts of anyone who tried to make any kind of breakthrough back to knowledge bases lost when the houses decided that they should start trying to nuke each other to see who gets to claim the most non-glowing planets and satellite factories.<br /> <br /> (Also also, I'm so used to people referring to Egyptian deities as furries out of hand and accustomed to referring to Daesh as just the IS that my first impulse upon reading the epithet &quot;furry Isis&quot; was to object to using the Greek in place of the original Egyptian name Aset.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:36:08-08:00","id":1186919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1186907#post1186907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it wouldn't be the same end, according to the tone used in the book. The Lunars changed. They aren't the Lunars of the First Age or the wars that came before it, because the loss of the Solars tore away something that could never be replaced.<br /> <br /> Edit: And chimerism doesn't seem to enter into the equation, because it's just mixing features on your totem animal. It's totally cool with just about every Lunar, and not a gateway to madness in this edition.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the developers have expressed dissatisfaction with framing the Silver Pact as something similar to Daesh. The parallels aren't really there; they grind up Artifacts that they can't use because otherwise they would die in droves. They're more a parallel of some theoretical faction in Mad Max that blows up old tanks and warheads and destroys fuel because they're really good at fighting without them, so they take advantage of this. Those Lunars of a more preservative bent, meanwhile, strike me as being kind of like ComStar from BattleTech, which hoarded technological secrets to try and keep together some semblance of interstellar relations going but would also covertly sabotage and/or co-opt the efforts of anyone who tried to make any kind of breakthrough back to knowledge bases lost when the houses decided that they should start trying to nuke each other to see who gets to claim the most non-glowing planets and satellite factories.<br /> <br /> (Also also, I'm so used to people referring to Egyptian deities as furries out of hand and accustomed to referring to Daesh as just the IS that my first impulse upon reading the epithet &quot;furry Isis&quot; was to object to using the Greek in place of the original Egyptian name Aset.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To kind of piggy-back on this a bit, I'm not a fan of the whole &quot;Solars are needed&quot; four a couple reasons.<br /> <br /> The first is that I kind of disliked the whole 1-to-1 thing of Solar-Lunars in 2e. To me the entire eidea of the Bond from 1e was something that Solars and Lunars, when it developed, happened to be something that was common and an emergent thing, not a hard-coded thing of Lunar Exaltation. The entire Bond idea to me worked better when it was a result of mutual trust, love, freindship/etc. that grew on its own terms and persists through lifetimes. The 2e take was that <i>every</i> Solar and Lunar had a pair, and that was set in stone before anyone had anything to say on it. That bothers me since it kind of robs to me the significance of it before, where it was soemthing more presonal you opted into rather than something foisted on you. It also has this bit of &quot;When everyone is specail, no one is&quot; to the anture to me.<br /> <br /> This also has an effect of kind of making Lunars feel overly &quot;dependent&quot; on Solars. This idea that a Solar Bondmate was proscribed by your Exaltation entirely to get your Caste just feels wrong ot me and not something that feels like Lunars would have been very happy with an ddoens't do a lot to me to feel like something you should strive towards.<br /> <br /> The second main issue is that it kind of misses the nature of the Lunar Castes as they are. Lunars thought Solars were gone forever. What they are now simply isn't what they were, and the entire process of smashing their Castes to rebuild them in 3e is meant to be an example of self-empowerment in the new Age that rose in the ashes of the Usurpation. It feels a bit against those themes to have Solars be an &quot;out&quot;, and it also kind of works against Lunar themes in their new write-up of them being a bit more forward-facing with them as kings. The Castes they have are for the Age they live in now. The First Age is dead, having a way to go back to it serves no use as the role those Castes reflect are to a society that no longer exists. I kind of see Lunars having this feel of evolving to take on the Age that it is. What they were in the First Age might not even be what htey were in the Divien Revolution, and what they might be in the next Age might be something else still. But I'm pretty sure 'backwards' just ins't in the Lunar volcabulary in their Castes.<br /> <br /> Lunar Castes are dependent on Solars in so much as what they are now is based on the loss of the Solars and the world order falling apart. The Solars return sin't a restoration of the First Age, and I don't think it really should be pushed as desirable to roll back when the Lunar identity for fifteen centuries is basically built on this diea that no, the Soalrs are explicitly <i>not</i> what defines Lunar sin this Age.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:45:32-08:00","id":1186921,"title":"","content":"And on other things, as noted, chimerism is just not a thing this edition like it was in 2e. Chimerism lets you become like, I dunno, this take on a &quot;giraffe&quot; based on the Roman accounts of a camel with the hindquarters and spots of a leopard and the neck and tongue of a serpent:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0743/1701/products/Proximo.jpg?v=1456893454\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0743/1701/products/Proximo.jpg?v=1456893454\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0743/1701/products/Proximo.jpg?v=1456893454\" target=\"_blank\"> https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0743/1701/products/Proximo.jpg?v=1456893454 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My gathering is that if you go this route you'll be seen maybe as an eccentric, but it's not like some critical case that you are going crazy this time around.<br /> <br /> The biggest things to me the Silver Pact offers young Lunars, besides the whole tattoos thing as a sign of general comraderie include:<br /> <br /> - Purpose since young Exalts are like, well young anyone so that's good.<br /> <br /> - Patronage of elders, which has probably enough perks in itself that folks don't need the gun of chimerism to join-up.<br /> <br /> - Promise of power and rulership. A big thing with the Lunar elders at least is this view, as I understand it, that they were Number Two. They ruled the world with only one group higher, the Solars. Now the Solars were gone, logic dictates the world is <i>theirs</i>. I'd say that's pretty motiviating in itself for folks blessed by a goddess, probably survived a Wyld Hunt, and probably grew up in some form of Realm-inflicted-poverty or oppression pre-Exaltation. There's a lot like, there for normal human motivations ot encourage Lunars to go agains thte Realm to me.<br /> <br /> And of course, not everyone signs-up. But well, enough do, and that's what matters for the Elders in the long run. They'll come along, die to a Wyld Hunt, or establish themselves and make due. The world is big, the emprie will die, the moon will rise, all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T04:16:07-08:00","id":1187000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1186868#post1186868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for a thousand years new Lunars received the not really a choice of &quot;sign up with Furry Isis and their war against China-Rome and the Astrology Jedis&quot; or &quot;succumb to Chimerism.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe developers have been clear on how the only drawback of not having a Caste is not having access to Caste Attributes and anima powers. Lunars can get by without tattoos fine.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, Lunars can get by with tattoos and then never again speaking to a Silver Pact member. The Silver Pact doesn't really have a means of forcing uninterested Lunars to do anything that they don't want to, so it's more of a mutual collective.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and the core book makes it clear that the tattoos are generally provided as a kind of common courtesy while carrying no other obligations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">young Exalts are like, well young anyone</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bNow I'm thinking about Kaneko... in a manner, I suppose he could be considered like a young person in the sense that he's not sure what to do with the rest of his life, but that was because he was quite sure that he was going to die shortly and had made peace with that.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T10:03:08-08:00","id":1187064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1187000#post1187000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNow I'm thinking about Kaneko... in a manner, I suppose he could be considered like a young person in the sense that he's not sure what to do with the rest of his life, but that was because he was quite sure that he was going to die shortly and had made peace with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mid-life or retiree crisis is a thing afterall. The Bull in a way is like the guy who retired, was kind of just throwing himself into things in the twilight of his life, and suddenly found something to keep him going longer. That just happened to be &quot;Be Genghis Khan&quot; in effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:28:54-08:00","id":1190108,"title":"","content":"So, I got a second wind on scribbling up some Lunar ideas. I'm curious what people's thoughts and themes might be on....<br /> <br /> How do you make Lunar Anima cool? Including Caste, MoonieTatts, and the like.<br /> <br /> What would you do with DBT? Still a scattering of Gift Charms buried in the trees, or reformat them into their own thing?<br /> <br /> How would a Beast-Boy Lunar be cool and effective? Instantaneous and/or partial transformations? Long-term or committed shapes? Some sort of shaping pool of motes or dice?<br /> <br /> What about Fury? Reorganized? Should it be a channeling of character-specific totemic power, or just being really angry? Is Fury a shapeshift of mindset, or something that isn't comparable?<br /> <br /> In a setting with Solar Sorcerers and Sidereal Astrologers, what makes a Lunar Occulty/Lorey brainiac special? Should (for lack of a better term) witchery or shamanism be a distinct experience? <br /> <br /> What would you do with territory? If we assume a normal, main-theme Exalted game is going to involve a lot of character travel, why would a Lunar get tied down somewhere? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T20:56:57-08:00","id":1190122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190108#post1190108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you make Lunar Anima cool? Including Caste, MoonieTatts, and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you make them NOT cool?<br /> <br /> Whenever you're about to do something awesome, a giant ghostly beast appears behind you to roar, howl, or shriek. In BlazBlue, the Lunar-like characters instead have magical glyphs appear which constitute extremely stylized depictions of their totem creatures.<br /> <br /> Your glistening, glowing tattoos can emphasize the lines of your muscles, accentuate your tiger stripes, draw attention to your sexual features, declare the story of how you earned your battle-name, or spiral into crazed patterns that bend the eye and drive the mind insane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would a Beast-Boy Lunar be cool and effective? Instantaneous and/or partial transformations? Long-term or committed shapes? Some sort of shaping pool of motes or dice? </div> </div> </div>First of all, some kind of discount for constantly changing shapes, to avoid getting mote-tapped.<br /> <br /> Second of all, the ability to flurry the shapeshifting action with an attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would you do with territory? If we assume a normal, main-theme Exalted game is going to involve a lot of character travel, why would a Lunar get tied down somewhere? </div> </div> </div>Something people rarely considered was how Second Edition Charms allowed a Lunar to pick any random location to become her territory instantly, or at least as soon she she could travel around its borders.<br /> <br /> Which meant that allowing a Lunar Exalt to pick the time and place of a confrontation could be extremely dangerous.<br /> <br /> ..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-28-2018, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T09:41:13-08:00","id":1190310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190122#post1190122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you make them NOT cool?<br /> <br /> Whenever you're about to do something awesome, a giant ghostly beast appears behind you to roar, howl, or shriek. In BlazBlue, the Lunar-like characters instead have magical glyphs appear which constitute extremely stylized depictions of their totem creatures.<br /> <br /> Your glistening, glowing tattoos can emphasize the lines of your muscles, accentuate your tiger stripes, draw attention to your sexual features, declare the story of how you earned your battle-name, or spiral into crazed patterns that bend the eye and drive the mind insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Impressions of Quote Slicing*<br /> <br /> All of that is very true. Do you make any mechanical changes to anima, tatts, or Caste to make them stand out as being particularly and uniquely Lunar? I was considering adding to the range of Lunar Caste perks, of which the Lunar themselves chose three during character generation. Perhaps with expansions to the breadth as the Lunar matures, but still three at a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, some kind of discount for constantly changing shapes, to avoid getting mote-tapped.<br /> <br /> Second of all, the ability to flurry the shapeshifting action with an attack. </div> </div> </div>If you were doing battle in your True Form, for instance, and you wanted to slash your enemy with tiger's claws, would that be a flurry to momentarily shapeshift, or a stunt, or an Instant Supplemental Charm, do you figure? <br /> <br /> Should assemble-on-the-fly or shift-on-the-fly be distinct from DBT or should it interoperate? I was considering presenting DBT and Gifts as the root of a tree, and ad-hoc shapeshifting as the root of a different tree. Thus, you could build a single truly monstrous Lunar war-form (Rawr I'm a werewolf!), or you could be ever-shifting and impossible to predict (Beast Boy with complete shapeshifts or terrifying chthonic monsters made of parts), but it would be difficult and expensive to do both at once. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something people rarely considered was how Second Edition Charms allowed a Lunar to pick any random location to become her territory instantly, or at least as soon she she could travel around its borders.<br /> <br /> Which meant that allowing a Lunar Exalt to pick the time and place of a confrontation could be extremely dangerous.<br /> .. </div> </div> </div>I was pulling from the concept of Lair in Beast, with the idea that a Lunar's Heart is the Elsewhere-place where their acquired shapes and shapeshift-melded stuff would appear. (Perhaps other Exalted with Elsewhere access have one too, but only Lunars and perhaps some others have such explicit access to it) To have other chambers, the Lunar would have to conclusively become the apex predator of the area, at which point they could connect it to their Lair. This would also build in some fast-travel that's distinct from other Exalted, and somewhat similar to waypoints. The Charms to create a temporary hideout would be extensions to this idea and potentially able to connect in as well. The cost of the coolness is that the Lunar would need to do some maintenance and have some involvement in their territories - not unlike and even closely in parallel to Solar (and other) social entanglements, but seen from a Lunar perspective.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T17:32:05-08:00","id":1190492,"title":"","content":"You're asking a lot of mechanical questions I don't think we can answer yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T17:34:42-08:00","id":1190493,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is all opinion, brainstorming, and homebrew that I'm asking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:06:11-08:00","id":1190527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190310#post1190310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pulling from the concept of Lair in Beast, with the idea that a Lunar's Heart is the Elsewhere-place where their acquired shapes and shapeshift-melded stuff would appear. (Perhaps other Exalted with Elsewhere access have one too, but only Lunars and perhaps some others have such explicit access to it) To have other chambers, the Lunar would have to conclusively become the apex predator of the area, at which point they could connect it to their Lair. This would also build in some fast-travel that's distinct from other Exalted, and somewhat similar to waypoints. The Charms to create a temporary hideout would be extensions to this idea and potentially able to connect in as well. The cost of the coolness is that the Lunar would need to do some maintenance and have some involvement in their territories - not unlike and even closely in parallel to Solar (and other) social entanglements, but seen from a Lunar perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though a lot of stuff with Beasts and their Lairs doesn't translate well to Lunars, because their dynamics in society and the tones of their stories are different.<br /> <br /> \u200bBeasts live in the World of Darkness, where the assumption is that most of the supernatural stuff is acting covertly, and so you've got their hidden nightmare realms that they get to pull people into that has a lot of metaphorical correspondences to them, which is also your way of still having the traditional monster lair in a world that might not have room for them.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhereas Lunars inhabit a world where they and powers in general get to be a bit more overt, and there are lots of blank spaces on the map, right down to the level of neighbourhoods of individual cities, where you can place a literal monster's lair. I also think that their predatory dynamic is sufficiently different from Beasts as to make an elaborate system based on secret fear mongering to not really be fitting to them (even if they can probably have some predatory nightmare powers that streamline a bit).<br /> <br /> \u200bOn a personal note, I wouldn't like the idea of Lunars having a metaphorical space in which their shapes exist, because I think that creates a sense of those shapes being a separate thing from them, which I don't think best serves them.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are other beings, possibly even other Exalted, that I think could draw a strong inspiration from Beast, but I think that for Lunars, they're best served by the territories that they can claim being literal places that they're empowered within.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough I may be misreading your point somewhat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T04:40:05-08:00","id":1190617,"title":"","content":"Possibly! It's an idea that I'm toying with, as something that's more interesting than activating a Charm to claim some territory. It also reminds me of moon paths, which is a concept that I really like. There's a bit of an idea in my head of being more powerful in a &quot;lair&quot; type of thing than a fortification type of thing, and that fearsome monsters can vanish into their lair type of thing. <br /> <br /> I do agree that the fearmongering is probably not a Lunar concept, nor is eating fear for dinner. <br /> <br /> Interesting point about the metaphorical space as being separate. I was contemplating a theme that having many selves opens up scenes where you might meet an interact with those selves, but I can see where that intent might be going off track.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the thoughts!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T06:07:13-08:00","id":1190633,"title":"","content":"A bit of explanation behind the form of Eska has given me a new perspective on the possibilities for Lunar hybrid forms.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor one thing, any criticisms I had in the past about adopting the war form for things other than fighting goes away when the purpose of the initial transformation is neutral, and turning it to combat is an additional layer of upgrade or transformation. Likewise, I'd even be enthusiastic about other Charms that specialize the hybrid form in different directions.<br /> <br /> I've been critical before of a power that just grants mutations (which are now Supernatural Merits), but if it's now the form of a basic Charm that can have power-ups and specialties built out of it, that makes it more acceptable to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd it's neat that there's an explicit departure in the aesthetics associated with it. I've thought of Lunar character concepts in the past myself who didn't really feel suited to the typical were-beast appearance; not that they had totems that weren't amenable to it, it just didn't fit the character I thought of. If the hybrid form can now accommodate the primarily humanoid with some feral or alien touches, that gives it a much broader application in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T06:11:51-08:00","id":1190634,"title":"","content":"I agree, it's far more flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T06:16:53-08:00","id":1190637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190634#post1190634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, it's far more flexible.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich also helps it fit into the more social, seductive Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T06:40:24-08:00","id":1190642,"title":"","content":"Although calling it &quot;Sexy Beastman Transformation&quot; might be a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T06:52:20-08:00","id":1190645,"title":"","content":"I like how it lets you build a Katana Catgirl.<br /> <br /> Enhanced Senses (Sight, Hearing) and Tail (one-dot) gets you a form with kitty eyes, ears, and tail, without fur or claws or digitigrade legs or fang-filled muzzle-jaws.<br /> <br /> Useful for swordplay more than for Brawl with natural weapons you don\u2019t need to buy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:02:56-08:00","id":1190647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190642#post1190642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although calling it &quot;Sexy Beastman Transformation&quot; might be a bit much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or only the beginning!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(At least it's not a spreadsheet, right? h/t that other thread)</span><br /> <br /> I did notice that Eska can increase Soak on a one-to-one mote basis but capped at half Attribute. That seems like an interesting mix of assumptions, though I suppose we'll have to see how that turns out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:22:02-08:00","id":1190652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190642#post1190642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although calling it &quot;Sexy Beastman Transformation&quot; might be a bit much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't like the name Sexy Beastman Transformation at all, but Daddy Beastman Transformation on the other hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:46:56-08:00","id":1190665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190647#post1190647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did notice that Eska can increase Soak on a one-to-one mote basis but capped at half Attribute. That seems like an interesting mix of assumptions, though I suppose we'll have to see how that turns out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably not something that applies to anything else.<br /> Obviously, Stamina's main purpose is soak; you use that far more than you actually make Stamina rolls (unless your game is all about surviving in the icy tundra, maybe). So the stamina excellency's not much use, compared to say the Dex excellency, if it can't boost soak.<br /> <br /> However, I remember one of the devs (maybe the previous ones, I can't remember) saying that that the issue is that if they did just let you boost soak up to your Stamina, there'd not be much point in buying soak-boosting charms. Since you could already get your soak up to 10 with Stamina 5 (15 with a stunt), which is as much as heavy armour.<br /> <br /> So I guess this is the compromise. You can boost your soak with just the excellency, but not very much. I imagine there's a low-essence charm that lets you boost the cap on how much you can increase your soak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:53:00-08:00","id":1190668,"title":"","content":"I think it's just treating soak as a static value like parry or dodge. Those already have a cap of half what you'd be able to add to a rolled value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T10:18:06-08:00","id":1190706,"title":"","content":"I think that it didn\u2019t seem to matter if the Stamina Excellency was narrow or even useless, since you get it for free.<br /> <br /> Unless Lunars DON\u2019T get them for free?<br /> <br /> Robert confirmed that DBT is a Strength Charm, but Eska doesn\u2019t have the Strength Excellency despite being a Full Moon.<br /> <br /> So getting a Lunar Attribute Excellency not as easy as learning one Charm based on that Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T11:01:09-08:00","id":1190722,"title":"","content":"Maybe they only get caste/favoured free? <br /> <br /> Or maybe DBT specifically doesn't get you it because it's so common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:53:41-08:00","id":1190753,"title":"","content":"My guess is it just takes more than one Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:02:41-08:00","id":1190760,"title":"","content":"Eska might not favor Strength, either.<br /> <br /> Maybe, as Full Moon, she was able to pick just Dexterity and Stamina?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:26:17-08:00","id":1190766,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've had confirmation that 3e lunars pick two caste out of three and two favoured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:40:21-08:00","id":1190773,"title":"","content":"It's a good system, we've been using it for years as a house rule and it works great. It also means they are picking approximately the same percentage of their caste attributes as Solars, actually, so it's fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:51:06-08:00","id":1190775,"title":"","content":"A bit of Exalted parody songwriting (if you can call it that) under the cut. I'd been sitting on it for two years, but it feels like it fits in better now!<br /> <br /> The Hybrid Form Is For War (original \u2013 \u201cThe Internet Is For Porn\u201d, from Avenue Q)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> Anja Silverclaws: As a No Moon, it\u2019s my task to teach our new fellows about their powers. I\u2019m going to teach them about something with untapped potential \u2013 the hybrid form!<br /> <br /> Anja: The hybrid form is really, really great!<br /> Strength of Many: For war!<br /> Anja: I\u2019ve got fast legs, so I don\u2019t have to wait!<br /> Strength of Many: FOR WAR!<br /> Anja: And I have such sharper sight!<br /> Strength of Many: FOR WAR!<br /> Anja: I stay alert all day and night<br /> Strength of Many: For war!<br /> Anja: It\u2019s like my body\u2019s made of light!<br /> Strength of Many: FOR WAR!<br /> Anja: Many!<br /> <br /> Strength of Many: The hybrid form is for war!<br /> Anja: MANY!<br /> Strength of Many: The hybrid form is for war!<br /> Anja: Strength of Many, please!<br /> Strength of Many: Why was this shape born? WAR! WAR! WAR!<br /> <br /> Anja: Many!<br /> Strength of Many: Oh, hello Silverclaws.<br /> Anja: You are ruining my tale!<br /> Strength of Many: Sorry, it wasn\u2019t intentional.<br /> Anja: Well, leave this to the No Moon, then?<br /> Strength of Many: Sure\u2026<br /> Anja: Now then\u2026<br /> <br /> Anja: I\u2019m glad we have this new morphology\u2026<br /> Strength of Many: For war!<br /> Anja: That gives us untold opportunity!<br /> Strength of Many: For war? Oops\u2026<br /> Anja: Seeing where ghosts have stopped\u2026<br /> Strength of Many: For-<br /> Anja: You can research, croon, and shop!<br /> Strength of Many: \u2026<br /> Anja: Until your ritual ends and you\u2019re ready to drop!<br /> <br /> Strength of Many: For war!<br /> Anja: No!<br /> Strength of Many: The hybrid form is for war!<br /> Anja: Many!<br /> Strength of Many: I\u2019m up all night goring with horns in war! War! WAR!<br /> <br /> Anja: That\u2019s a waste of potential!<br /> Strength of Many: Sticks and stones, Silverclaws!<br /> Anja: No, really, it\u2019s so short-sighted. Other castes don\u2019t just think about clashing in a contest of might!<br /> <br /> Strength of Many: Oh?<br /> Anja: What?<br /> Strength of Many: You have no idea. Ready, other castes?<br /> <br /> Red Jaws: Ready!<br /> Seven Devil Clever: Ready!<br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater: Ready!<br /> Last Hunter of Xaal: Ready!<br /> <br /> Strength of Many: Let me hear it!<br /> All but Anja: The hybrid form is for war!<br /> Last Hunter: The rush of this shape is great!<br /> All but Anja: The hybrid form is for war!<br /> Last Hunter: I eviscerate!<br /> All but Anja: The hybrid form is for war! War! WAR!<br /> <br /> Anja: Hold on a minute! I happen to know that you, Red, use your hybrid form to track prey.<br /> Red Jaws: Aye.<br /> Anja: And you, Seven, use it to keep watch on your neighborhood.<br /> Seven Devil Clever: Yeah.<br /> Anja: And you, Gerd-rhya, appear to your people as a figure of power!<br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater: This is correct.<br /> Anja: And you, Last Hunter-rhya, use it to weave structures at amazing speed!<br /> Last Hunter: That is a truth.<br /> <br /> Strength-of-Many: But Anja, what do you think he does\u2026 after he sets up his web?<br /> Last Hunter: I earned my name for good reason.<br /> Anja: Damnit!<br /> <br /> All but Anja: The hybrid form is for war! <br /> The hybrid form is for war!<br /> They call it \u201cDeadly\u201d quite rightly<br /> For war! War! WAR!<br /> The hybrid form is for<br /> The hybrid form is for<br /> The hybrid form is for war!<br /> <br /> Anja: I don\u2019t need that form, anyway! I\u2019m leaving!<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T17:57:31-08:00","id":1191183,"title":"","content":"With the hybrid form, my concept of the &quot;Oni&quot; Ox-Tiger Chimera is even better realized.<br /> <br /> His hybrid form can be red- or blue-skinned, and his only animalistic features could be an oni's ox-horns and tigerlike fangs and claws.<br /> <br /> <br /> Harpies, centaurs, mermaids, lamia... It's like an episode of My Life With Monster Girls!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T23:59:49-08:00","id":1191274,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t tell if you\u2019re being glib or sincere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T03:04:45-08:00","id":1191295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1190753#post1190753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is it just takes more than one Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure, but that is plausible. After all, Lunar excellencies cover far more than Solar ones, so maybe you need 2 or 3 charms from an attribute to get the excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T05:23:39-08:00","id":1191310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191274#post1191274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can\u2019t tell if you\u2019re being glib or sincere...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't make a sincere statement with a feeling of humor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:56:56-08:00","id":1191443,"title":"","content":"Anyone else want to discuss the possibility that Lunar Exalted <i>might </i>get the ability to combo their native Charms freely with Martial Arts Charms? And the possible balance-point that Lunar Exalted <i>might </i>be stuck at the Terrestrial-level of Martial Arts Charms?<br /> <br /> I think that would be really neat. All Martial Arts traits are Abilities, and Lunar Exalted don't learn magic based on Abilities. Being able to learn Martial Arts Charms at all seems like a stretch for them.<br /> <br /> But being able to combo those Charms with their native Attribute Charms would really help represent the archetype of &quot;unskilled, but so strong it doesn't matter&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T14:16:53-08:00","id":1191449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191443#post1191443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else want to discuss the possibility that Lunar Exalted <i>might </i>get the ability to combo their native Charms freely with Martial Arts Charms? And the possible balance-point that Lunar Exalted <i>might </i>be stuck at the Terrestrial-level of Martial Arts Charms?<br /> <br /> I think that would be really neat. All Martial Arts traits are Abilities, and Lunar Exalted don't learn magic based on Abilities. Being able to learn Martial Arts Charms at all seems like a stretch for them.<br /> <br /> But being able to combo those Charms with their native Attribute Charms would really help represent the archetype of &quot;unskilled, but so strong it doesn't matter&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Terrestrial Keyword doesn't seem to rely on skill. Technically, the Dragon-Blooded derive their polish from expertise in skill, but they get saddled with a limitation, which seems to be about raw power. It's not a simple case of &quot;Mastery reflects great skill, therefore Terrestrial must mean lesser skill&quot;; the two down and up-gunning Keywords seem to be following different axes in terms of themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T17:28:39-08:00","id":1191485,"title":"","content":"You can have the lunars use the terrestrial keyword because ability-based charms are a bit alien to them while having the DBs use it for entirely different reasons that are more to do with raw power. <br /> <br /> The only thing that feels weird is that it would mean none of the main four exalt types would naturally be neutral towards martial arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T18:47:07-08:00","id":1191499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191485#post1191485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that feels weird is that it would mean none of the main four exalt types would naturally be neutral towards martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals.<br /> <br /> They don't get Mastery effects naturally; they have to go through some trick to do that, just as Dragon-Blooded need to elevate themselves to neutrality through the Immaculate Dragon Styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T21:00:27-08:00","id":1191522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191485#post1191485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have the lunars use the terrestrial keyword because ability-based charms are a bit alien to them while having the DBs use it for entirely different reasons that are more to do with raw power.<br /> <br /> The only thing that feels weird is that it would mean none of the main four exalt types would naturally be neutral towards martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, again, that the Terrestrial keyword description means that the premise for doing it doesn't make much sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T21:09:57-08:00","id":1191524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191522#post1191522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, again, that the Terrestrial keyword description means that the premise for doing it doesn't make much sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This keyword denotes that a Martial Arts Charm grants a lesser or restricted effect when used by Dragon-Blooded martial artists. Certain masters of the Immaculate Order have developed spiritual initiations that allow them to overcome these limitations.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't see what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> Not unless you're arguing that the keyword doesn't make sense if it applies to Lunars as well as Terrestrials. But that's a minor concern, since it's a system keyword and not a part of Creation's nomenclature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T21:21:28-08:00","id":1191529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191524#post1191524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;This keyword denotes that a Martial Arts Charm grants a lesser or restricted effect when used by Dragon-Blooded martial artists. Certain masters of the Immaculate Order have developed spiritual initiations that allow them to overcome these limitations.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't see what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> Not unless you're arguing that the keyword doesn't make sense if it applies to Lunars as well as Terrestrials. But that's a minor concern, since it's a system keyword and not a part of Creation's nomenclature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiritual practices in Exalted are at least fairly in line with some notion of power and enlightenment. Lunars blow past where Dragon-Blooded are because of what they get from Luna in terms of command over their own Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T00:06:49-08:00","id":1191559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191529#post1191529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spiritual practices in Exalted are at least fairly in line with some notion of power and enlightenment. Lunars blow past where Dragon-Blooded are because of what they get from Luna in terms of command over their own Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they have greater command over their own essence in general, it's not impossible that they could have roughly equal command for using martial arts, as the Lunars don't use Ability based charms, so could plausibly use the Terrestial keyword. It could go either way: using the Terrestial keyword or not using the Terrestial keyword are plausible options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13611-metalrift","name":"Metalrift","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T04:56:58-08:00","id":1191594,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think of the Martial Arts as Ability Charms. They're codified and functional in their own right, and you have only to be taught them. <br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's worth keeping in mind that the Terrestrial Keyword is less about metaphysics then it is about mechanical balance; you have an effect that is too strong compared to their other powers, so you tone it down a bit.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like the image of the Martial Arts as a form of power open to beings that is largely unreserved. If Lunars being able to combine their Charms with Martial Arts unbalanced them, I'd sooner drop that line of development then say that the Terrestrial Keyword applies to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T07:08:00-08:00","id":1191612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191594#post1191594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't think of the Martial Arts as Ability Charms. They're codified and functional in their own right, and you have only to be taught them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ability-based Exalted get a Martial Arts Ability Excellency, with a dice-adding limit based on the rating of their Ability for that Style.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded don't get one for free, so they have to use the special Brawl Excellency they need to purchase.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted wouldn't get one at all. They'd just use their Dexterity Excellency, along with the Excellency of whatever Attribute a Martial Arts Charm calls upon for a special (Attribute + MA) roll. And even then, their dice-adding limit would be entirely based on their Attribute rating and totally ignore their Martial Arts rating for that Style.<br /> <br /> That definitely seems like a case of &quot;so strong it doesn't matter how skilled I am&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T07:27:17-08:00","id":1191616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191612#post1191612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ability-based Exalted get a Martial Arts Ability Excellency, with a dice-adding limit based on the rating of their Ability for that Style.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded don't get one for free, so they have to use the special Brawl Excellency they need to purchase.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted wouldn't get one at all. They'd just use their Dexterity Excellency, along with the Excellency of whatever Attribute a Martial Arts Charm calls upon for a special (Attribute + MA) roll. And even then, their dice-adding limit would be entirely based on their Attribute rating and totally ignore their Martial Arts rating for that Style.<br /> <br /> That definitely seems like a case of &quot;so strong it doesn't matter how skilled I am&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't know what point is being made here.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: All right, I thought about it, and I think I can see what it's getting at with the idea of different Excellencies showing different priorities in a group's power.<br /> <br /> But I don't think reading Lunars in terms of &quot;stronger than they're skilled&quot; is the right approach for that.<br /> <br /> \u200bLunars can still develop Abilities to 5. They can still be good at things, and it probably helps them to be so. They don't get magic from it, but I think that's because their magic has a different priority, not because they're intrinsically averse to skill.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think that matters to the Martial Arts, because that's not their own magic.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr perhaps more accurately, I don't think that's a strong enough argument against them being able to use Martial Arts to the mid-level, which is the thing I want that the system already seems geared towards. Martial Arts are codified fighting and spiritual techniques for generically harnessing one's energy, and Lunars have more energy than Terrestrials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-04-2018, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T08:51:27-08:00","id":1191626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191594#post1191594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't think of the Martial Arts as Ability Charms. They're codified and functional in their own right, and you have only to be taught them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>are </i>charms requiring a minimum rank of Martial Arts ability, and <i>usually</i> require a +Martial Arts roll to resolve the effect (esp, Attacks and Parries). <br /> <br /> Usually. Although witness that Tiger Style, for instance, uses Strength rank to measure a lot of its effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:14:45-08:00","id":1191630,"title":"","content":"Woopdms, removed! Sorry, hahah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":23657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","user":"VioletDreamer","date":". 03-04-2018, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:44:45-08:00","id":1191638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191630#post1191630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Nephrwacks still only access the first Circle of Necromancy, or do you plan to allow more things to access the Second Circle of Necromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wrong thread, friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:38:29-08:00","id":1191668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191626#post1191626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>are </i>charms requiring a minimum rank of Martial Arts ability, and <i>usually</i> require a +Martial Arts roll to resolve the effect (esp, Attacks and Parries).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFine, for the sake of closing all of the possible loopholes against which some &quot;Um, actually&quot;s might slip through:<br /> <br /> \u200bMartial Arts are not Exalted Ability Charms, and exist in the setting as codified magical extrapolations from martial techniques, largely irrespective of the kind of Exalted (and other beings) who are using them. They use the Martial Arts Ability, which functions differently from every other Ability in that you need to buy a special Merit to even use it, it needs to be bought separately for every Martial Art, and Exalted who use Ability Charms cannot develop their own Martial Arts Charms (with the exception of Excellencies, which are barely Charms). Hence, the difference between being Attribute and Ability Exalted should not be relevant for learning the Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Somebody remind me, because my memory on the point is a bit shaky; are the Getimian Exalted not going to be Attribute Exalted? You know, the &quot;Rakan Thulio thinks they're better at this then the damn Sidereals&quot; Exalted?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:42:18-08:00","id":1191672,"title":"","content":"I agree with Isator. I can't really see that a Snake-totem Lunar shouldn't be allowed to be at least reasonably good at Snake Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:43:15-08:00","id":1191698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191672#post1191672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Isator. I can't really see that a Snake-totem Lunar shouldn't be allowed to be at least reasonably good at Snake Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is five dots and all Snake Style Charms not \u201creasonably good\u201d at Snake Style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T12:28:14-08:00","id":1191713,"title":"","content":"&quot;Good with&quot; is probably enough, and &quot;Good at&quot; less of a concern. I think it's a fun idea to amplify the feel of having sort of rough edged Attribute magic that doesn't gel easily with Lunar power.<br /> <br /> I guess the concerns I would have are that a) it could be awkward for the developers to implement to still make MA sufficiently &quot;worth it&quot;, and b) it imposes more systems mastery on Lunar players to find synergies between MA Charms and Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> (Though I would say if your goal is to have conflicts play out in game where Lunars are using levels of MA Charms that Dragonblooded can't (Dynasts be all &quot;Huh! what! huuh! No, how can this be!&quot; in classic corny style), then yes, that would blunt that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T11:02:23-08:00","id":1191995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191443#post1191443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else want to discuss the possibility that Lunar Exalted <i>might </i>get the ability to combo their native Charms freely with Martial Arts Charms? And the possible balance-point that Lunar Exalted <i>might </i>be stuck at the Terrestrial-level of Martial Arts Charms?<br /> <br /> I think that would be really neat. All Martial Arts traits are Abilities, and Lunar Exalted don't learn magic based on Abilities. Being able to learn Martial Arts Charms at all seems like a stretch for them.<br /> <br /> But being able to combo those Charms with their native Attribute Charms would really help represent the archetype of &quot;unskilled, but so strong it doesn't matter&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that thematic point already going to be covered by the fact that Lunars <i>don't get favored abilities</i>. This means raising ability scores is going to be hideously expensive in character generation (4 points just to max out a single ability! that's more than a quarter of your total BPs <i>for a single ability!</i>), and both hideously expensive <i>and</i> time-consuming out of it (five weeks to get to ability 5 alone - if you decide to go for a second MA, your campaign might be over by the time you'd train up just the ability, nevermind picking Charms to go with it). You will also have to pay more for the Charms themselves.<br /> <br /> I think the cumulative effect of this will be <i>in typical play </i>(ie. outside of heavy min-maxing environments) that most Lunars will fulfill the &quot;unskilled but so strong it doesn't matter&quot; niche simply by not having as many MA Charms (and sometimes even MA dots) as an equivalent-xp ability exalt. (I, at least, would certainly not bother with getting MA 5 on anyone but a dedicated martial artist if I was playing a Lunar - consequently, this would lock me out of about half of every tree in the game because grumble grumble stupid overinflated ability prerequisites grumble.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T09:52:02-08:00","id":1192645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1191698#post1191698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is five dots and all Snake Style Charms not \u201creasonably good\u201d at Snake Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point, so I'll rephrase it.<br /> <br /> I think a Snake Totem Lunar with snake style should be better than a Dragonblood with snake style. <br /> <br /> Not to mention, as Aluminiumtrioxid just mentioned, they're going to be paying more XP for the ability than most other martial artists*, and the charms are going to be unfavoured. <br /> <br /> I don't actually expect that combo-ing MA and Lunar charms is going to be a big balance issue, but at the end of the day, I'd rather say they can't combo the charms (except excellencies) than say a Lunar punching someone with a Tiger charm uses the Dragonblood level.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I assume, as I assume they won't have any favoured abilities. Actually, in 2e, they got Survival and one other as favoured. Which meant 75% of Lunar PCs I saw had Martial Arts favoured anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T09:59:46-08:00","id":1192648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1192645#post1192645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...in 2e, they got Survival and one other as favoured. Which meant 75% of Lunar PCs I saw had Martial Arts favoured anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in 2e you needed Martial Arts to effectively claw and bite people, because there was no separate Brawl. It is a slightly different beast in 3e being separated out again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T10:09:20-08:00","id":1192653,"title":"","content":"Oh, indeed. Starting with Martial Arts 5 for maximum clawing was one of the reasons, but having cheaper access to more charms (which favouring no other ability gave you) was part of it too.<br /> ut if Lunars use the same system as Solars this edition (if you favour Brawl, you favour Martial Arts) then I think you'll find 75% favouring Brawl (for the clawing and biting) and thus also favouring Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> But I assume they won't this time. Could be wrong!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T10:57:08-08:00","id":1192667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1192653#post1192653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, indeed. Starting with Martial Arts 5 for maximum clawing was one of the reasons, but having cheaper access to more charms (which favouring no other ability gave you) was part of it too.<br /> ut if Lunars use the same system as Solars this edition (if you favour Brawl, you favour Martial Arts) then I think you'll find 75% favouring Brawl (for the clawing and biting) and thus also favouring Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> But I assume they won't this time. Could be wrong!</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't get you a quote right now, but I'm pretty sure Vance outright said they won't get favored abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T11:12:29-08:00","id":1192671,"title":"","content":"The points about unfavored costs are sound.<br /> <br /> I suppose a Lunar ability to combo Attribute and Martial Arts Charms would be balanced not only by the inability to favor any Martial Arts Ability, but also the inability to achieve Mastery-level effects or learn Sidereal Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T18:50:49-08:00","id":1192901,"title":"","content":"Vance confirmed: No favored Abilities.<br /> <br /> He also confirmed that a new Lunar could gain a substantial tell in the form of a Supernatural Merit. So, if you wanted your basic human character to get kitty ears as a Tell, you can do that, and they'll be at least as functional as Enhanced Sense: Hearing.<br /> <br /> And then you can spend the limited points of Hybrid Body Transformation on <i>other</i> Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, you know how Enhance Sense: Smell requires some obvious sign? I figured out that if you want Enhanced Sense: Smell without getting a muzzle (as with Natural Weaponry 3/4 dots), you can just do with a wet black nose-tip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:31:39-08:00","id":1193062,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here comes a thought. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Eska's charms, <i>Octopus and Spider Barrage</i>, and <i>Instinct-Driven Beast Movement</i>, both give added benefits when in appropriate <i>animal forms</i>, (of which </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">is explicitly <i>not</i> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the Hybrid Body Rearrangement form). The Ask the Devs thread also asserts that Lunars will be able to access form enhancements -- such as supersizing insectoid forms, and air-breathing-mermaiding aquatic forms.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like the indications that the devs are putting thought into making more animals forms playable and providing insentives to utilise them.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-08-2018, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:00:12-08:00","id":1193300,"title":"","content":"Oh, absolutely. I suspect there'll be plenty of other charms that are better in certain forms, and these will be quite varied, so that it's useful to have a variety of forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1192901#post1192901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance confirmed: No favored Abilities.<br /> <br /> He also confirmed that a new Lunar could gain a substantial tell in the form of a Supernatural Merit. So, if you wanted your basic human character to get kitty ears as a Tell, you can do that, and they'll be at least as functional as Enhanced Sense: Hearing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a good move, because honestly, a lot of the tells people think of are, essentially, supernatural merits. Such as animal ears, tails, fangs, unusual eyes (my No Moon had owl's eyes, for example, so they should probably have a bonus to seeing at night), etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:11:47-08:00","id":1193304,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'd put too much stock in it, but looking at Eska, I see her attributes are 9/4/6.<br /> Which is the starting attributes of Lunars in 2nd ed: 8/6/4+1. Which I felt seemed fair, with them getting 1 more dot of attributes and 3 less dots of abilities than Solars.<br /> Or maybe they get the same as Solars and she just bought 1 more dot. Can't really tell. But they don't seem to get a lot more than Solars at the start, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:09:57-08:00","id":1193326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1193304#post1193304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'd put too much stock in it, but looking at Eska, I see her attributes are 9/4/6.<br /> Which is the starting attributes of Lunars in 2nd ed: 8/6/4+1. Which I felt seemed fair, with them getting 1 more dot of attributes and 3 less dots of abilities than Solars.<br /> Or maybe they get the same as Solars and she just bought 1 more dot. Can't really tell. But they don't seem to get a lot more than Solars at the start, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I miss first edition's 9/7/5 spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T00:01:52-08:00","id":1193454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1193304#post1193304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'd put too much stock in it, but looking at Eska, I see her attributes are 9/4/6.<br /> Which is the starting attributes of Lunars in 2nd ed: 8/6/4+1. Which I felt seemed fair, with them getting 1 more dot of attributes and 3 less dots of abilities than Solars.<br /> Or maybe they get the same as Solars and she just bought 1 more dot. Can't really tell. But they don't seem to get a lot more than Solars at the start, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember how tertiary attributes are cheaper to buy in chargen than primary and secondary ones? I'm guessing Lunars will be able to buy up their caste and favored attributes at the same cost as well (or maybe &quot;instead of&quot;, because this method could be cheesed very easily for a price break on effectively all attributes - but if this happens, they better get <i>something </i>to make ability purchases less painful).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:50:50-08:00","id":1193529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1049263-thinking-about-3e-lunars?p=1193326#post1193326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I miss first edition's 9/7/5 spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do the people I play with, but that's why I thought it's notable. I don't know if it's 8/6/4 like Solars, or 8/6/4+1 like 2e Lunars, but it's definitely not 9/7/5.<br /> But tbh, I think 9/7/5 is probably a bit good. A lot of the Lunars I see have all their attributes at 4 or 5 because it's pretty easy to get them high. My own No Moon's stats in 2nd ed were 4/4/4/4/5/4/5/5/4, which I think is probably a little silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminimtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember how tertiary attributes are cheaper to buy in chargen than primary and secondary ones? I'm guessing Lunars will be able to buy up their caste and favored attributes at the same cost as well</div> </div> </div> </div>They could in 2e. It was 3 points for favoured attributes. Which is... okay? I mean, Solars get a 50% reduction in the cost of their ability dots, so giving Lunars a 25% reduction for their attribute dots doesn't seem over-generous.<br /> <br /> But because of the way attribute dots are split between 3, rather than 25, and you can raise them above 3 without spending freebies, it gets a bit weird.<br /> For example, if you are a Full Moon who favours Dex and Strength, but not Stamina and put your 8pts into physical, then decide to put 12 freebies into raising your favoured attributes, you actually end up with Str5/Dex5/Sta5, even though you don't favour 5.<br /> It's not a big problem, just a bit odd.<br /> I guess this is what you meant by:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminimtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">because this method could be cheesed very easily for a price break on effectively all attributes</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... but it's not actually that cheesy.<br /> <br /> I definitely don't think they should lose the slight reduction on tertiary attributes though. Putting up tertiary attributes costs significantly less XP later than putting up primary attributes.<br /> <br /> And, sure, you can spend 15 freebies to get 9 tertiary attributes instead of 4, but what's wrong with that? That in no way seems more broken than a Solar starting with 7 abilities at 5 (and one at 4), which the game kind of encourages you to do.<br /> <br /> Essentially, aside from a bit of WP and some merits, and maybe raising like one ability (say, Occult for a sorcerer, or Brawl for a Full Moon) to 4 or 5, there isn't much to spend your freebies on besides attributes.<br /> <br /> Considering that Solars can get 12xp worth of ability dots for 2 freebies, I don't at all see it as a big deal with Lunars spending 3 freebies to get 6-16xp worth of attribute dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since Vance has said they will no longer get favoured abilities, I think we can be confident they won't get &quot;something to make ability purchases less painful&quot; because, well, that'd be what favoured abilities would do.<br /> And as long as they get a reduction on attributes, that seems fine to me. <br /> <br /> I'm quite happy for Lunars to start with plenty of attribute dots but few abilities higher than your normal skilled mortal warrior/trickster/shaman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:59:23-08:00","id":1193534,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, I suspect the easiest thing is just to say Lunars can buy all attributes at 3 points a dot. That stops people trying to game the system (which isn't exactly hard), and doesn't encourage min-maxing quite so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}